  "foaf:name": "ALAN and Warming Impacts on Marine Interactions",
  "sdo:name": "ALAN and Warming Impacts on Marine Interactions",
  "sdo:description": "Light pollution is a growing threat to coastal habitats worldwide and is increasing in intensity and extent at an unprecedented rate. Increasingly, however, coastal ecosystems are exposed to multiple stressors, which can co-occur and have additive or interactive effects. Understanding interactions between light pollution and ocean warming on marine species – both widespread stressors that impact important sensory cues and biological processes – allows managers to prioritise sensitive areas and can buffer marine habitats against the forecasted impacts from climate change. By assessing impacts from microbes to seaweeds, sea urchins and fish, this project provides a holistic understanding of how ALAN – independently and combined with other stressors – impacts the marine environment and the consequences to ecosystem functioning and the future provision of key services.",
